rules_dotnet: `named_resources`, embedded resources under an explicit name

A file listed in `resources` is always embedded as
`<assembly name>.<path in the package, with dots>`. MSBuild does not name
resources after the assembly: it uses the project's `RootNamespace` (which is
the assembly name only by default), the full name of the class a `.resx` file
belongs to, or `LogicalName` metadata. Code finds a resource by that name
(`ResourceManager`, `Assembly.GetManifestResourceStream`), so a project whose
assembly is called `Contoso.Common` and whose root namespace is `Common`
compiles under rules_dotnet and then finds none of its resources at run time.

Add `named_resources`, a dict from file to logical name, next to `resources`
on the C# and F# library, binary and test rules. Each entry is passed to the
compiler as `/resource:<file>,<name>` (`--resource:` for F#) and is an input of
the compile. `resources` keeps its naming.

Made against rules_dotnet 0.22.2. Apply with -p1.

diff --git a/dotnet/private/common.bzl b/dotnet/private/common.bzl
index b0846ea..6ea8559 100644
--- a/dotnet/private/common.bzl
+++ b/dotnet/private/common.bzl
@@ -776,6 +776,25 @@ def copy_files_to_dir(target_name, actions, is_windows, files, out_dir):
 _RESOURCE_TEMPLATE_CSHARP = "/resource:{}"
 _RESOURCE_TEMPLATE_FSHARP = "--resource:{}"
 
+def collect_named_resources(named_resources):
+    """Resolve a `named_resources` attribute to the files it names.
+
+    Args:
+        named_resources: (dict[Target, str]) The value of the attribute.
+
+    Returns:
+        (dict[File, str]) Each file to embed and its logical name.
+    """
+    result = {}
+    for target, logical_name in named_resources.items():
+        files = target[DefaultInfo].files.to_list()
+        if len(files) != 1:
+            fail("named_resources: {} must be exactly one file, got {}".format(target.label, len(files)))
+        if not logical_name:
+            fail("named_resources: {} has an empty logical name".format(target.label))
+        result[files[0]] = logical_name
+    return result
+
 def map_resource_arg(file, target_label, out_dll, language):
     """Map an embedded resource file to a resource argument for the compiler.
 
diff --git a/dotnet/private/rules/common/attrs.bzl b/dotnet/private/rules/common/attrs.bzl
index 322c378..d94c634 100644
--- a/dotnet/private/rules/common/attrs.bzl
+++ b/dotnet/private/rules/common/attrs.bzl
@@ -50,6 +50,19 @@ COMMON_ATTRS = {
         # that is generated by a dotnet binary
         cfg = default_transition,
     ),
+    "named_resources": attr.label_keyed_string_dict(
+        doc = """Files to embed in the DLL as resources under an explicit logical name: file -> name.
+
+        A file listed in `resources` is named `<assembly name>.<path in the package, with dots>`.
+        MSBuild derives the name from the project's `RootNamespace` (which need not be the
+        assembly name), from the class a `.resx` file belongs to, or from `LogicalName` metadata,
+        and code finds a resource by that name (`ResourceManager`, `GetManifestResourceStream`).
+        Use this attribute when the name has to be a particular one. Each key must be a single file.
+        """,
+        allow_files = True,
+        # See the comment on `resources`.
+        cfg = default_transition,
+    ),
     "out": attr.string(
         doc = "File name, without extension, of the built assembly.",
     ),
